{"name":"Water Lily","hex":"#dde3d5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"water lily","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various members of the Nymphaeaceae family that are tuberous plants, rooted in soil with leaves (lily pads) and flowers floating on the water surface.","Species of genus Nymphoides, fringed water lily and similar plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water_lily"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nymphaeaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Nymphaeaceae is a family of flowering plants, commonly called water lilies. They live as rhizomatous aquatic herbs in temperate and tropical climates around the world. The family contains five genera with about 70 known species. Water lilies are rooted in soil in bodies of water, with leaves and flowers floating on or rising from the surface. Leaves are oval and heart-shaped in Barclaya. Leaves are round, with a radial notch in Nymphaea and Nuphar, but fully circular in Victoria and Euryale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG/330px-Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeaceae"},{"title":"Nelumbo","blocks":[{"text":"Nelumbo is a genus of aquatic plants with large, showy flowers. Members are commonly called lotus, though the name is also applied to various other plants and plant groups, including the unrelated genus Lotus. Members outwardly resemble those in the family Nymphaeaceae, but Nelumbo is actually very distant from that family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Nelumno_nucifera_open_flower_-_botanic_garden_adelaide2.jpg/330px-Nelumno_nucifera_open_flower_-_botanic_garden_adelaide2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelumbo"},{"title":"Water Lily (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"The Water Lily is a cocktail made with gin, crème de violette, orange liqueur such as triple sec or cointreau, and fresh lemon juice. It can be garnished with orange zest and served in a coupe glass."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_Lily_(cocktail)"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering Barclaya longifolia specimen, Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg/330px-Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg/330px-Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flower of Victoria cruziana, Santa Cruz water lily","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictoria_cruziana_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg/500px-Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg/1280px-Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg/500px-Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering Euryale ferox specimen cultivated in the Botanischer Garten Berlin-Dahlem, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEuryale_ferox_kz06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg/500px-Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg/1280px-Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg/500px-Nuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.vari-002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering and fruiting Nuphar variegata specimen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANuphar_variegata_15-p.bot-nuphar.v